    REFERENCE-RESOLUTION FACTS, MEASURED ON A LIVE PDI - READ THIS FIRST
    This case row carries the pinned number CASE9000010.

    The package uses two reference shapes, decided by measurement rather
    than taste. This row uses shape B only:

      B. assigned_group (a sys_user_group), assigned_agent (a sys_user)
         -> key in the display_value attribute AND in the element body.
         sys_user and sys_user_group reference bodies are never checked by
         preview (a deliberately bogus user_name produced no problem), and
         the import engine DOES resolve them: the demo users, the demo
         group and the three sys_user_has_role rows all landed on the
         instance under these artifacts' own sys_ids with their user and
         role references correctly resolved. These columns therefore
         commit LINKED (assigned_group by name, assigned_agent by user_name)
         and need no post-commit repair.

    AAP Section 0.5.2 requires every cross-reference to resolve by a stable
    human-readable key (case by number, user by user_name, group by name,
    company by name) and forbids a literal sys_id in any reference field.
    The shape above carries the key, never a sys_id, so it complies.
    The 9,000,000 number band sits far above anything the CASE / TASK /
    PARTY counters issue, so a pinned number cannot collide with a
    counter-issued one, and the counter itself is left untouched.

    Demo Case 10 - Closed / Complaint / Critical priority
    ====================================================================

    Synthetic seed record for the case-management POC scoped application.
    This file is the LAST and FINAL of the 10-case demo dataset; together
    with cases 01 through 09 it satisfies the AAP requirement (Section
    0.7.4) of "at least 10 demo cases across all six statuses and both
    case types," and completes the dataset matrix:

        Case 01 - Draft       / General Inquiry / Medium
        Case 02 - Open        / General Inquiry / Medium
        Case 03 - In Progress / General Inquiry / Medium
        Case 04 - Pending     / General Inquiry / Low
        Case 05 - Resolved    / General Inquiry / High
        Case 06 - Closed      / General Inquiry / Medium
        Case 07 - Open        / Complaint       / High
        Case 08 - In Progress / Complaint       / Critical
        Case 09 - Resolved    / Complaint       / High
        Case 10 - Closed      / Complaint       / Critical   ## THIS FILE

    The 10-case dataset thus exercises:
      * Every one of the six statuses (Draft, Open, In Progress, Pending,
        Resolved, Closed)
      * Both case types (General Inquiry and Complaint) across the
        full lifecycle
      * All four priorities (Low, Medium, High, Critical) - this case
        is the SECOND of two Critical-priority cases (the other is
        case 08), ensuring the all_cases_by_priority Manager View bar
        chart has a non-empty Critical bar with diverse statuses

